# Waste Segregation Using CNN and IoT

## Project Overview
This project uses a Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) to classify waste images into organic and non-organic categories and estimate their decomposition time. It combines deep learning with hardware integration to support smarter waste segregation.

## Technologies Used
- Python
- TensorFlow and Keras
- CNN-based image classification
- Google Colab
- Visual Studio Code (VS Code)
- Flask API
- ESP32-CAM
- Arduino IDE

## System Workflow
1. The CNN model processes waste images and predicts the waste category.
2. The predicted category is used to estimate the decomposition time.
3. The Flask API provides an interface for communication between the model and the application.
4. The ESP32-CAM serves as the camera hardware for capturing waste images.

## Key Features
- Organic and non-organic waste classification.
- Estimated waste decomposition time.
- CNN-based image recognition.
- API-based communication using Flask.
- Camera-based waste image capture using ESP32-CAM.

## Objective
To develop a smart waste segregation system that combines deep learning and camera-based hardware to encourage proper waste disposal and environmental awareness.

## Future Enhancements
- Improve classification accuracy.
- Expand the number of waste categories.
- Enhance real-time hardware integration.
- Develop a user-friendly interface for displaying predictions.
